         text="Two Venetian merchants, Buono of Malamocco and Rustico of Torcello, took the body of the evangelist from his church in Alexandria and smuggled it aboard under a load of pork, which Muslim customs men would not touch. Doge Giustiniano Partecipazio received it; a chapel was built beside his castle to keep it, and the lion of Mark became the city's sign.",
