         text="The galley Angelo Gabriele rowed into the basin trailing captured Turkish banners in the water: the Holy League had destroyed the Ottoman fleet at Lepanto on 7 October, more than a hundred of its galleys from Venice's Arsenal. Bells rang for days; shops closed, and the Piazza was lit and hung with Turkish trophies.",
