         text="A fire swept through the halls of the Great Council and the Scrutinio, destroying paintings by Guariento, Gentile and Giovanni Bellini, Carpaccio and Titian. Some wanted the Gothic palace rebuilt in the modern style; the Senate chose to restore it as it was, and Tintoretto, Veronese and Palma painted the new ceilings and walls.",
